<title>SPAIN: Spain Q3 GDP rose 2.2 pct y/y, 0.6 pct q/q - INE.</title>
<headline>Spain Q3 GDP rose 2.2 pct y/y, 0.6 pct q/q - INE.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute gave the following figures, 1986 prices (pctg change):</p>
<p> GROSS DOMESTIC PRODUCT	    Q3 '96   Q2 '96    Q3 VS Q2 '96</p>
<p>					    yr/yr    yr/yr	qtr/qtr</p>
<p> Gross domestic product	     2.2	 2.0	  0.6</p>
<p> Private consumption		  2.0	 1.8	  0.6</p>
<p> Public sector consumption	  0.9	 1.1	  0.1</p>
<p> Gross fixed capital formation   -0.4	 1.1	 -0.6</p>
<p>    Capital goods		     8.4	 6.4	  1.9</p>
<p>    Construction		     -5.3	-2.0	 -2.1</p>
<p> Variation in stocks		  0.2	 0.2	  0.2</p>
<p> Internal demand			1.5	 1.7	  0.3</p>
<p> Exports				  9.4	 8.3	  2.6</p>
<p> Imports				  6.6	 7.0	  1.4</p>
<p>NOTE - Q2 figures may be revised. GDP was revised from 1.9 pct</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
